{
  "dom_id": "step-q114148",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+11 \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+\\phantom{1}8x-\\phantom{1}4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-3x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,11x-4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{11x-11}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{3{x}^{2}+8x-4}{x-1}=$",
  "worked_solution": "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+11 \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+\\phantom{1}8x-\\phantom{1}4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-3x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,11x-4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{11x-11}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $3{x}^{2}+8x-4$ by the linear binomial $x-1$ gives\n\n- the quotient $3x+11,$ and\n\n- the remainder $7.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}+8x-4}{x-1}=3x+11+\\frac{7}{x-1}.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
